    {
      "@type": "Book",
      "@id": "https://milos-timotijevic.github.io/books/vek-sumnje-religioznost.html#work",
      "url": "https://milos-timotijevic.github.io/books/vek-sumnje-religioznost.html",
      "name": "Век сумње: религиозност у чачанском крају 1886–2008",
      "alternateName": [
        "Век сумње: религиозност у чачанском крају: 1886–2008",
        "Vek sumnje: religioznost u čačanskom kraju 1886–2008",
        "A Century of Doubt: Religious Life in the Čačak District, 1886–2008",
        "A Century of Doubt: Religiosity in the Čačak Region, 1886–2008"
      ],
      "description": "Историјска студија јавног испољавања религиозности у чачанском крају од 1886. до 2008. године. Књига прати промене у односу појединца, Цркве, друштва и државе, кризу религиозности под утицајем модернизације, међуратне покушаје обнове православне побожности, социјалистичку секуларизацију и атеизацију и постсоцијалистичку обнову јавне религиозности.",
      "abstract": "A historical study of publicly expressed religiosity in the Čačak region from 1886 to 2008. Using a localized microhistorical approach to test broader patterns, the book examines the changing relationships among individuals, the Serbian Orthodox Church, society and the state. It follows the decline of public religious practice around the turn of the twentieth century, interwar attempts at re-Christianization associated especially with Bishop Nikolaj Velimirović and the Bogomoljci movement, socialist secularization and atheization after 1945, and the post-socialist revival of public piety and religion in political and everyday communication. The study distinguishes formal religious identification and public religious manifestation from regular liturgical practice and also addresses popular piety, modernization, church public discourse and invented tradition.",
      "genre": [
        "Scholarly monograph",
        "Social history",
        "Cultural history",
        "History of religion",
        "Historical anthropology",
        "Microhistory",
        "Local history"
      ],
